      "message": "I think we already set `ALLOW_MISSING_DEPENDENCIES`. https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/orchestrator/inner_build/inner_build_cf_vendor.py;l\u003d33. \n\n\nCurrently for Multi-tree, this has the affect of not raising an exception during Soong analysis, buts it adds the paths to `MissingDependencies` https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/soong/android/paths.go;l\u003d1132?q\u003dPathForSource. Therefore the ninja file turns out to be\n\n```\nbuild foo: g.android.error\n desc: \"foo is missing prebuilt_lib.so\"\n```\n\n`prebuilt_lib.so` will always be missing from the inner_tree\u0027s build graph (atleast in clean build), since it will be generated by the orchestrator",
